VeridianOS: fix compiler warnings in kcursorgen and the Breeze style

GCC reported:

- -Wunused-function for the five Options::*() functions in
  cursors/src/kcursorgen/options.h, compiling kcursorgen.cpp. The functions
  are static (internal linkage) and only main.cpp uses them; kcursorgen.cpp
  included the header without using anything from it. The unneeded include
  is removed from kcursorgen.cpp.
- -Wunused-parameter for 'corners' in Helper::renderStaticTabBarTab()
  (kstyle/breezehelper.cpp). The static tab is drawn with plain rectangles,
  unlike renderTabBarTab(), which rounds the given corners; the parameter
  exists to keep the two signatures alike. It is marked Q_UNUSED, as the
  file does for other such parameters.

Behaviour is unchanged.

diff -ru a/cursors/src/kcursorgen/kcursorgen.cpp b/cursors/src/kcursorgen/kcursorgen.cpp
--- a/cursors/src/kcursorgen/kcursorgen.cpp	2026-10-08 17:01:25.682065386 -0400
+++ b/cursors/src/kcursorgen/kcursorgen.cpp	2026-10-08 17:03:36.129721341 -0400
@@ -4,7 +4,6 @@
 */
 
 #include "kcursorgen.h"
-#include "options.h"
 
 #include <QCollator>
 #include <QDebug>
diff -ru a/kstyle/breezehelper.cpp b/kstyle/breezehelper.cpp
--- a/kstyle/breezehelper.cpp	2026-10-08 17:01:25.707209293 -0400
+++ b/kstyle/breezehelper.cpp	2026-10-08 17:03:38.630702331 -0400
@@ -1303,6 +1303,9 @@
                                    Corners corners,
                                    qreal animation) const
 {
+    // static tabs are drawn with square corners
+    Q_UNUSED(corners)
+
     bool enabled = stateProperties.value("enabled", true);
     bool hovered = stateProperties.value("hovered");
